window.SOLACE_PAGES = {"00-home":"# SOLACE\n**21+ · Conan Exiles · RP / PvP / PvE**\n\n## An exile is more than their sentence.\nBuild a home. Find your people. Start something worth remembering.\n\nSOLACE is an English-language Conan roleplay community for players who want more than a race to the strongest weapon. A lonely camp can become a trading post. An argument can start a feud. A lost fight can become the beginning of a better story. Spend your evening in the tavern, hunt a bounty, set up a clan, study forbidden magic or simply make a life for your character.\n\n**Start your story** → `/start`  |  **Read the rules** → `/rules`\n\n### Find your place\n- **The World**: Conan-inspired, lore-conscious stories with space for both quiet nights and real consequences.\n- **Eight Professions**: Bard, Bounty Hunter, Medic, Fighter, Thief, Alchemist, Slaver and Courtier.\n- **Three Special Classes**: Sorcerer, Blacksmith and Wise, with quest- and ritual-based development.\n- **Mechanical PvP**: Skill-based combat, with clear intent and post-fight consequences.\n- **The Hub**: Shops, services, work, stories and a strict warning for those who start trouble inside town.\n- **Living Economy**: Trade, crafting, daily silver and weekly gold.\n\n## Our promise\nA lively world is not the same as a world that revolves around one faction. Nobles, wanderers, craftspeople, merchants and troublemakers should all find reasons to log in. Your character can face consequences without your place in the community becoming disposable.\n\n### What SOLACE is not\nNot a mandatory kingdom storyline. Not dice-based PvP. Not a permanent safe zone. Not a place where a staff member's character decides an OOC dispute involving their own group.\n\n**[Discord invitation, add official URL]** · **[Server address/status, add when configured]**\n","01-start-here":"# Start Here\n*Your first evening shouldn't feel like homework.*\n\n## Before you join\n1. SOLACE is **21+** and English-speaking. Join the official Discord and follow the onboarding/whitelist instructions posted there.\n2. Read **General Rules**, **Roleplay & Character**, **PvP**, and **Consequences & Consent** before playing. If you want to build, read **Building & Storage**. If you want conflict, read **Raids** too.\n3. Create a lore-appropriate adult character. Use a Conan culture from `/races`; do not assume your origin grants automatic stat boosts or obligatory enemies.\n4. Complete the consent form when available. Your boundaries should be known before a difficult scene begins.\n5. Choose a profession based on the kind of roleplay you want to invite. Professions are distinct from advanced classes.\n6. Learn the PvP intent and surrender procedure before leaving the starter area.\n7. Visit the Hub for markets and everyday social roleplay; read the **Hub attack warning** before causing violence there.\n8. Need a break or leaving Discord? Open a ticket to notify staff rather than simply disappearing.\n\n## New player checklist\n- [ ] Read the rulebook and 21+ entry requirements.\n- [ ] Joined Discord and completed required application details.\n- [ ] Character has a plausible name, origin, motivation and adult age.\n- [ ] Read IC/OOC, metagaming, recordings and consent rules.\n- [ ] Know how to initiate, join or surrender in PvP.\n- [ ] Chosen a profession. Characters with a Class must also have one.\n- [ ] Asked staff if a custom lore element or prohibited build area is unclear.\n\n## Quick questions\n**Can I avoid RP while gathering?** You are considered IC outside the designated starting zone. Do not use OOC status to evade encounters. Communicate briefly and respectfully if a real-life interruption happens.\n\n**Is this a dice-combat server?** No. Mechanical PvP is the combat default. Some specialist non-combat abilities use separate RP success systems.\n\n**Can I record the game?** Not for OOC intelligence or distribution of private scenes. See `/privacy` for limited promotional sharing.\n\n**Where is the game IP?** [Publish after hosting is active.]\n","02-world":"# The World of SOLACE\n## A place for the stories between battles\nThe Exiled Lands are harsh. The people living in them don't have to be one-dimensional. SOLACE welcomes ambitious chiefs, cautious traders, scholars, innkeepers, solitary hunters, travelling healers and criminals who understand that trouble follows them home.\n\n### Player-made stories, lasting results\nYour choices create opportunities for other characters. Diplomacy can keep a village alive. Raiding a rival has costs. An enemy who survives may become a useful ally or a lifelong rival. PvP supports roleplay; it is not an excuse to write everyone else's story for them.\n\n### Conan first\nThe base setting is Conan's Hyborian world. A custom location or exceptional concept must be reviewed against Conan lore and the active server map. Refer to `/races` for a starting point, not an exhaustive canon encyclopedia.\n\n### A town with a pulse\nThe Hub is where traders, entertainers and adventurers cross paths. It hosts player markets and planned profession activity. It allows PvP, but attacking inside the city carries a uniquely severe consequence: read `/hub`.\n\n### Play your own pace; respect others' time\nQuiet RP is real RP. So is war. People on either side are here to build stories together. Distinguish your feelings from your character's grudges, and respect the boundaries established through consent.\n","03-rules-general":"# General Rules\n**Draft v0.1 | SOLACE rulebook with owner-approved amendments.**\n\n## At a glance\nSOLACE is a 21+ English-speaking roleplay community. Stay in character where required; keep IC conflict out of OOC spaces; do not metagame, exploit, harass, troll, evade bans or recruit players to other servers through this community. Staff decisions should be documented. [Read PvP →](/rules/pvp) · [Consent →](/rules/consequences)\n\n### G-01: OOC player disputes\nPlayers are expected to handle minor disagreements maturely. Staff is not a personal mediator for every argument. Use Discord block and a calm direct conversation when appropriate. Persistent harassment, rule breaking, and IC/OOC blending belong in a ticket with evidence. The directly affected player normally submits a harassment complaint; see the emergency reporting and staff-report routes in `/support`.\n\n### G-02: Age and conduct\nParticipation in SOLACE is **21+**. Player characters must also be adults in body and mind. No underage/childlike sexual themes. No discriminatory slurs, targeted hatred, stalking, deliberate harassment, griefing or trolling. Follow Discord's community guidelines as well as site rules.\n\n### G-03: Discord presence and account identity\nMembership in the official Discord is required to play. Keep application details accurate and open a ticket before leaving Discord or taking an extended absence. Unannounced departures are handled through the documented account/character process; don't assume staff can preserve access if they cannot identify your character. No unreported alternate accounts or ban evasion. Household players and Discord-account transfers require a ticket.\n\n### G-04: The spirit of the rules\nA missing technical loophole is not permission to abuse other players or the server. Rule lawyering, bad-faith debate and exploitation of wording may lead to staff action. Staff may address harmful conduct not exhaustively itemized in these pages under the published community principles. Formal decisions must still be recorded with reasons and an appeal route; emergency safety measures are treated separately.\n\n### G-05: IC and OOC are separate\nYour character may lie, plot, fight or fall in love. That is not permission to harass the player behind another character, pressure someone to change a scene in private messages, or call OOC allies into an IC dispute. Use IC means for IC retaliation. Discuss required consent and practical coordination OOC without manipulating outcomes.\n\n### G-06: Recruitment and advertising (Poaching)\nDo not use SOLACE spaces, private recruitment directed at its members, or server events as an advertising funnel for another server. Do not actively poach players from another community in SOLACE's name. Friends may choose to play together without being coerced or advertised to.\n\n### G-07: Recordings, screenshots and streaming\nA recording of an encounter cannot be used as IC intelligence. Do not secretly observe streams, distribute private scenes or pass footage to uninvolved players for in-game advantage. Screenshots/clips may be retained confidentially for evidence. Promotional highlights and community content may be shared under the permission and privacy rules on `/privacy`. Recording itself is not a way around metagaming restrictions.\n\n### G-08: Investigation and discipline\nStaff may review suspicious roleplay and take proportionate, temporary protective measures where needed. **A disciplinary decision requires explainable supporting findings**, not suspicion alone. Confirmed conduct, allegations and interpretation must be kept distinct. Investigators must recuse themselves when their own character/faction is involved. Use `/support` for decisions and appeals.\n\n### G-09: Server and platform integrity\nNo exploits, scripts, dupes, deliberate lag, mesh abuse, unlawful access, alternative-account circumvention, combat logging or bypassing approved game mechanics. Notify staff privately if you find an exploit rather than demonstrating it in public. Do not use a ticket as permission to keep exploiting something.\n\n### G-10: Current version controls\nThe published rule revision and effective date govern. Emergency platform/player-safety responses may be immediate. Permanent or material rule changes should be announced and ordinarily apply prospectively; the amendment log will state any exception.\n","04-roleplay-and-characters":"# Roleplay & Characters\n*Write your character, not someone else's.*\n\n## Quick rules\nYou are IC outside the designated starter area. Use local chat and appropriately emoted whispers for RP; clan chat is OOC. All roleplay communication must be in English, with a translation if you use another language. Do not use modern terminology, copied pop-culture characters or anachronistic songs in IC scenes. Original characters should fit Conan lore.\n\n## How we write together\n- **Metagaming:** putting OOC knowledge into your character's decisions; includes recordings, private Discord intel and teleporting to information your character has not learned.\n- **Metaposing:** claiming to know another character's unspoken intent or writing their action for them.\n- **Godmodding:** deciding another player's character must obey or has already been hit without a valid mechanic/consent.\n- **Powergaming:** refusing a reasonable response window or using mechanics to close off all replies.\n- **Blending:** transferring IC affection, hostility or revenge onto real players.\n\nDescribe **attempts**, and allow other characters to respond. Don't force a character to react to your thoughts. Be courteous about posting order in a large scene. If life interrupts, explain briefly OOC in whisper and arrange a sensible pause; do not disappear to evade a difficult consequence.\n\n## Immersion, language and lore\nKeep names, behavior and character concepts plausible in the Conan setting. Lore-based strengths and flaws, once part of an approved character concept, should actually be played. Modern slogans, anachronistic media, famous fantasy names and out-of-world references may be moderated. Questions about culture, appearance or rare concepts belong in a lore/character ticket.\n\n## Character basics\n- Player eligibility: 21+. Character must be an adult in physical and mental presentation (18+ minimum in the legacy character rules; SOLACE entry itself is 21+).\n- Use a setting-appropriate in-game **first name** for logging; surnames and honorifics can be used in RP where appropriate.\n- Character and clan names must suit the setting, not imitate a famous character or existing franchise protagonist.\n- Keep anatomy and sliders within believable approved character specifications. For very unusual appearances, ask staff before creation.\n- Gender-diverse character concepts are welcome. Avoid fetishizing gender identity and ask staff when a proposed magical transformation requires a custom lore exception.\n- All characters must remain playable and follow any approved class/character limitations.\n\n## IC/OOC chat\nRP in local or whispered chat with an emote establishing what your character is doing. Use OOC whispers or designated channels for practical notes, such as an urgent pause or a consent clarification. Clan chat is not an IC telepathic network; a raven, runner or approved in-world ability must convey IC information.\n\n## Eavesdropping and stealth\nSeeing text appear in local chat does not prove you were physically close enough to hear it. Walls and multiple doors stop ordinary hearing. Capture evidence of viable positioning if information may later matter in a dispute. When stealth is plausible and one character OOC notices another, the observer rolls perception and the hidden character responds with stealth; a person standing visibly in the open needs no discovery roll. This is an RP tool, **not dice PvP**.\n\n## /act appearance descriptions\nUse `/act` to describe visually identifiable features, especially while disguised. State clothes, build and relevant visible markers: e.g. `Scarred traveller in a sand-coloured hood`. Don't use secret character names, unexplained titles or vague descriptions to evade identification.\n\n## No banned content\nNo sexualized underage content, sexual content with animals, or other prohibited content under server/platform policy. A mature setting does not remove consent or platform limits. No unwanted sexual content can be imposed through a success roll or prior IC conduct. Sensitive RP boundaries are detailed on `/rules/consequences`.\n\n## Character reroll\nGive a new character at least **7 days** before requesting a normal reroll, unless staff grants an exception. Using the initial 7-day reroll places the account on the inherited **30-day reroll cooldown**. Open the relevant ticket and disclose ongoing conflict. A dispute that has been pursued within the preceding **5 days** may count as active; staff decides whether a contest is genuine. Rerolls are announced through the accountability process. Parties normally have a **24-hour** opportunity to contest an unresolved story, but a contest cannot be used as an excuse to demand a free kill. The inherited fuller process allows up to **48 hours after reroll** for a qualifying contest; see the published staff process for timing. A new character must not join revenge or resurrection RP concerning the old character's death. Self-perma requires staff approval and is not a means to dodge a conflict. Timers reset at a new wipe, subject to unresolved conflict review.\n\n## Character shelving\nPlayers have the inherited **two standard character shelves**. A living shelved character cannot be brought back for **30 days** (SOLACE change from the legacy 60). Earned research/mastery/merits are retained where the configured systems support preservation. A deceased character intended for later approved resurrection must be shelved. Custom/RP-acquired race eligibility is **not** automatically inherited; check current Conan-specific application policy. Notify staff before leaving Discord or becoming absent.\n\n## Pregnancy\nPregnancy is not actively played in SOLACE (meeting direction inherited from prior reference). Where needed for an agreed long-term story, use an appropriate shelving request; no pregnancy RP as a shield against active conflict. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: whether the legacy next-season return requirement is retained in full.]\n\n**Related:** `/races` · `/professions` · `/rules/consequences` · `/support`\n","05-pvp":"# PvP Rules\n**Mechanical PvP is the default combat resolution. SOLACE does not use dice PvP.**\n\n## The 30-second answer\nAn aggressor declares an RP intent and the server's PvP-intent command. Everyone within the applicable local range must make their initial **Join** or **Surrender** response. Once all affected people have declared **Ready**, the initiating player starts the countdown. You cannot summon late allies into an already active fight. There is one home-base defense exception detailed below.\n\n## 1. Where PvP is possible\nYour character is IC and PvP can occur throughout the map, except the designated starter zone and other expressly published protected technical locations. **The Hub permits PvP but applies its own sharply restricted outcomes.** Read `/hub` before you initiate there.\n\n## 2. Exact initiation sequence\n1. Give a clear IC emote explaining the threatening act and write `(PvP Intent)`; issue the approved server command (legacy example: `/pvpintent`, subject to bot implementation).\n2. Everyone affected stays stationary during declaration, except where a published character merit expressly permits a limited move. Any such movement is declared with its merit.\n3. Everyone within the intent's local range responds with a brief emote and **Join** (`/pvpjoin`) or **Surrender** (`/pvpsurrender`). Join includes the right to flee once the fight begins; Surrender means no mechanical fight and the character enters the applicable consequence stage.\n4. Players confirm `Ready` or `R` when declarations have finished.\n5. Initiator runs `/pvp start` to begin the **10-second** start timer. Fight only after the countdown ends. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: which installed plugin provides these exact commands; do not show nonfunctional slash commands as live instructions.]\n\n## 3. Nearby people and late joining\nA bystander within the original initiation range must respond to the initial intent. **After combat becomes active, no new participant may join from outside.** The sole exception: if the character who was attacked successfully reaches **their own base**, characters already **inside that base** may take part in defending them. They may not teleport to create artificial reinforcements. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: what counts as 'inside', and how staff records the exception.]\n\n## 4. Winning, losing, surrendering\nAfter being mechanically downed, do not rejoin the battle. Return promptly to the down location if the game's death/respawn system requires it, kneel or lie there and apply the configured injured status. Downed players cannot continue combat. The standard consequence phase follows unless a specific zone overrides it. Leaving a downed player without RP for **30 minutes** after PvP ends permits them to leave still injured; for battles of **10+ players**, that unattended limit is **45 minutes**.\n\n## 5. Teleport, mounts, terrain and movement\n- No portals, wayshrines or warps in the approach to an active fight, in the fight or during consequences, save the permitted technical return to a downed body. You cannot initiate/join a fight for **15 minutes** after a warp.\n- No mounted combat. Dismount immediately if intent is made, and put your mount on guard.\n- A fleeing player must evade active pursuit for **10 minutes** before the fight ends. A new encounter afterwards requires a fresh initiation. Having eluded pursuit does not grant an instant return warp; reach your base by normal travel where the inherited rule requires it.\n- Water cannot be looped for healing or damage avoidance. Pursuers may attack a fleeing target in water; a fleeing player may not turn the water into an attack exploit. Cross by the shortest sensible route and do not repeatedly re-enter the same water source.\n- Do not change locks, relocate decoration, dismantle or exploit building pieces after intent/raid initiation. Lock changes outside combat must be clearly emoted and interruptible.\n- Height sliders: in the legacy mechanical-PvP accommodation, a character shorter than **171** adjusts to **171–189** after initiation and restores their RP appearance afterwards. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: mod/slider scale.]\n- No spawn/warp camping. Stay at least **20 foundations** from public spawns/warps when patrolling and don't linger to stage an ambush.\n- If flying is available through a mod, land within **4 foundations** of an active intent and do not use flight to initiate an ambush.\n\n## 6. Abilities, dungeons, combat effects\nAn aggressive spell/merit/ability used around others must be properly emoted to give them a chance to respond; the recipient may treat it as intent. Mechanical spells/abilities are allowed during active PvP and in PvE where they do not affect other players. On leaving an instance during an active fight, move at least **5 foundations** clear of the entrance before attacking; do not use the loading zone to heal/camp cooldowns. A fleeing participant cannot return to the same instance for **30 minutes** or until the fight has ended, whichever inherited restrictions apply. Where a public event is formally tagged **KOS**, follow the event notice and record your join; *there is no blanket KOS permission outside advertised KOS events.*\n\n## 7. After the fight\nRegular world encounters use `/rules/consequences`. The Hub has different and more severe rules **for the aggressor who loses**, and only Injury is permitted as a winning aggressor's consequence in the Hub. Raid battles additionally use `/rules/raids`.\n\n## Example: a chase back home\nA is initiated on the road. A joins and flees; the fight has already started. A reaches their **own base**. Only defenders already inside that base may now enter under SOLACE's narrowly defined exception. Friends who receive a Discord message, spawn elsewhere or warp across the map may not join.\n","06-consequences-and-consent":"# Consequences, Captivity & Consent\n**A lost fight should create a story, not take away a player's real-world boundaries.**\n\n## What follows a defeat?\nRegular-world PvP may lead to an injury, disarming, robbery, agreed enslavement, marking, dismemberment or justified permadeath, depending on the appropriate stage and limitations. No consequence can be used as OOC retaliation. The **Hub is a separate exception**: a victorious aggressor there may apply **Injury only**, not robbery or kidnapping. See `/hub`.\n\n## Consent comes first for sensitive content\nSOLACE will use a **Consent Form** so players can specify permitted, conditional and refused categories before participating in heavy RP. Enslavement and Slave Breaking require the affected player's explicit OOC consent. Non-consensual sexual content is never generated by a mechanical/rolling result or treated as automatically accepted because of earlier IC acts. Consent can be clarified or withdrawn; agree a compatible non-sensitive story result where appropriate. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: publish the actual consent form and category labels.]\n\n### Fade to Black (FTB)\nIf all parties have **already agreed** the consequence, they may skip depiction of a scene, agree what took place and play its aftermath. FTB is not an escape from an otherwise valid agreed IC consequence, but it is **not** permission to impose an expressly refused sensitive act. Communication is required so both sides leave with the same understanding.\n\n## Standard consequence structure\nThe inherited introduction specifies a maximum of **one Primary and three Secondary** consequences, with no duplicate consequence on the same character. **The source later conflicts with this and says any number may be applied subject to exceptions**; until this is resolved by the owner, use the conservative one-Primary/three-Secondary ceiling as a clearly identified **publication hold**, not a covert staff interpretation. Permadeath is a sole outcome; a Primary consequence spell cannot be stacked with another Primary spell, and no more than three Secondary spells are allowed. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: authoritative limit.]\n\n### Primary examples\nSignificant injury (above Moderate); major dismemberment when allowed; Primary Robbery; defined Primary consequence spell; consensual enslavement where it is governed as a major consequence.\n\n### Secondary examples\nModerate injury; scarring/marking and defined minor mutilation; Secondary Robbery; defined Secondary consequence spell.\n\n### The inherited robbery tables\nOnly take permitted categories, after a valid world encounter, with a proper RP emote. These **legacy currency/material item names require mapping to SOLACE's actual economy**:\n\n| Primary robbery, choose one | Amount/condition |\n|---|---|\n| Gold | 6 |\n| Gems | 5 |\n| Gem Dust | 60 |\n| Advanced Research Pages | 2 |\n| Item with Power Rating | 1, only from the second PvP encounter |\n| Special Jewelcrafting/Apothecary Reagent | 1, only from the second PvP encounter |\n\n| Secondary robbery, choose one | Amount/condition |\n|---|---|\n| Gold | 3 |\n| Gems | 3 |\n| Gem Dust | 40 |\n| Weapons/armour | 3 gear pieces |\n| Other resources | 5 stacks of unlisted items |\n| Scrying clue | One item of clothing/object, emote-only is sufficient |\n\nPlayer-crafted, enchanted and potion-category objects need the inherited one-special-item restriction rather than being counted as disposable stacks. Robbery can include emote-supported inspection of mount inventory, not OOC reading of hidden items. **A Thief may take items from a player's base**: up to **2 stacks** per chest, leaving a discoverable **POI**, with a **6-hour** tracking window and a record of the RP. Outside of this, base property is only taken in a valid raid.\n\n## Injuries and restraint\nA downed character receives the configured **Slightly Injured** status and cannot run away, fight again or recover via external aid against the victor's will during consequence processing. Where not attended after combat, the 30/45-minute unattended rule in `/rules/pvp` applies. Restraining a downed player takes one appropriate emote; freeing a restrained player requires an initiating emote, a **5-minute** wait, then a second emote. A defeated character may be narratively disarmed without claiming a forbidden robbery; they cannot use a new weapon before reaching home under the inherited rule. Injury severity and magic/healing limitations must be respected.\n\n## Captivity: SOLACE amendment\n**Server rule, for every character: captivity lasts 24 hours.** During that time, captors who remain active must provide the captured player with at least **2 hours of actual RP**. If the capturing party is active and fails to provide that RP within the window, the captive is free to leave. **Long-term captivity or enslavement is allowed when both players agree.** Everything happens with the player's consent, and consent can be withdrawn. The immediate consequence phase after a fight is **3 hours**, unless extended by mutual agreement. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: clock starting event, paused server outages and how a captive reports an unattended session.]\n\n## Slaver: Break Will and Truth Compulsion\nWith the target player's advance OOC agreement, each **successful** Breaking use contributes **1/3**. Three successful uses on the same target make them **Broken**. Failures do not add progress. No roll overrides the actual player's consent. The meaning, duration, removal, maximum frequency and permitted orders of Broken are **under design** and must not be fabricated by the website.\n\n**Truth Compulsion:** a Slaver may force a consenting captive to answer questions truthfully. Like every captivity rule, it needs the captive player's OOC consent.\n\n## Permadeath (PK/PD)\nThe most consequential outcome needs a reason tied to existing IC events. Open a **Permadeath Request** before the fatal emote; normally a first encounter does not authorize forced permanent death. An exceptional first-encounter request must be approved in advance. In a genuinely immediate exceptional scene, open a documented ticket and leave the body intact for admin review rather than precluding a possible *left for dead* decision. Permadeath cannot be stacked with additional consequence types. 'No Value of Life' is contextual, not automatically proven by refusing an unreasonable demand or behaving consistently with an approved culture/flaw. Do not perma-kill uninvolved clan members simply because their leaders lost. A related admin/faction member must not be the deciding reviewer.\n\n**Critical hub warning:** Starting PvP in the Hub and losing puts your character under the NVL rule: the person you attacked may kill you, take you as a slave, or have you jailed in the Hub. Read `/hub` before attacking anyone there.\n","07-raids":"# Raids & Sieges\n*A raid is a conflict scene with a goal, not an offline inventory purge.*\n\n## Before you declare\n- No offline raiding. Show a current screenshot that proves at least **40%** of the defending clan's **active** members are online (e.g. 4 of 10). Members inactive for two weeks were excluded from the legacy percentage calculation; SOLACE's membership removal now occurs after **three weeks**, so staff must distinguish calculation activity from clan-removal status.\n- Have a clear IC objective: e.g. recover a captive, breach a rival's fort or confront an enemy leader.\n- Open a **Raid Ticket** naming the defending clan, attacker clan, any attacker allies, and the objective.\n- An uninvolved staff observer must approve and supervise. Once approved, both sides receive **1 hour's warning**; this conveys only the IC knowledge of an approaching unknown force to the defenders, not a free OOC alarm to all neighbors.\n- Scheduling follows staff coverage; the old rules prioritize **18:00–00:00 EST** but SOLACE must publish the actual moderation window and timezone. Raids at unreasonable off-hours for the target population may be declined. **[CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: staff timezone/coverage.]**\n\n## During the raid\n1. Once declared, no portal/warp/wayshrine for either side. A defender may use the explicitly permitted **home warp to defend home**.\n2. Attackers may arrive on mounts but keep them away from the raid scene; no mounted combat.\n3. Attackers must travel from their declared location and reach the target within **10 minutes after the raid start timer** or risk cancellation and a **24-hour** attempt cooldown.\n4. A raid uses the regular mechanical PvP protocol and post-fight consequence rules unless a raid-specific exception applies. **SOLACE's no-late-joining rule still governs**, except successful retreat into the defender's own base enabling those already inside to help defend.\n5. No rebuilding, dismantling or repairs after the initial **30-minute** pre-raid phase, except permitted siege equipment present before the raid. Doors/gates may be opened, closed, locked or unlocked according to the rule; no geometry manipulation.\n6. All music boxes at the raid location must be turned off to reduce mechanical stutter.\n\n## Loot and cooldowns\nA raider does not automatically empty the defender's base. If defenders **flee their defense**, each raider may take up to **one inventory at 100% encumbrance** under the inherited rules; staff controls chest access. Research pages and ritual reagents have a separate inherited limit: **2 research pages and 1 ritual reagent per raider**, capped at **5 raiders** for that allowance. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: map these item categories to installed SOLACE mechanics.]\n\nAfter raiding a clan, attackers have a **3-day cooldown** before raiding that clan or the participating defenders again. This inherited cooldown does not apply to defenders who initiate a counter-raid, and it does not arise if defenders flee under the source-specific exception. Thief lockpicking is limited to **two entrants** without an approved full raid; see `/professions/thief`.\n\n## Information and staff conduct\nDo not watch a raid OOC or share live Discord/stream intelligence. IC calls for help require a messenger, raven or another actually available lore-approved in-world communication, documented as needed. Staff players may take part in faction conflict but a person whose character/faction participates cannot moderate, approve, observe as referee or adjudicate that raid. If no uninvolved observer is available, postpone the raid.\n\n## No Hub raid\nThe Hub can have ordinary PvP with its own consequences, **never a declared Hub raid or siege**. See `/hub`.\n\n### Raid ticket checklist\n`Defender clan` · `Attacker clan` · `Attacker allies` · `IC objective` · `Online active-member evidence` · `Proposed time / target timezone` · `Independent staff observer`.\n","08-building-and-storage":"# Building, Clans & Storage\n*Build a believable place people can actually visit.*\n\n## Main building rules\n- Every player, including a solo player, must use a clan for tracked building and storage. Maximum inherited clan size: **12 players**.\n- A clan may have **one permanent base**. Temporary small RP camps/outposts must be removed after use unless staff grants extra time. No second permanent storage base.\n- Maximum height without permission: **10 wall heights**. No foundation spam: normally up to **2 foundation layers** for uneven terrain, at most **3** where genuinely needed; use walls/pillars otherwise.\n- No honeycombing, empty-room door mazes, thermal-effect trap spam, impossible floating structures or other raid-resistance exploits.\n- Cliff and raised bases need believable non-climbing access such as stairs; islands need a bridge, unless a specifically approved technical concept applies. Underwater/elevator-only sections cannot house otherwise unreachable protected storage or be exploited during conflict.\n- Do not block main routes without an accessible alternate passage. Do not build outside the green wall, under the mesh or in instanced dungeons. Keep marked POIs and protected zones clear.\n- Large clans (**5+ members**) cannot build within **3/4 map grid** of another large base, and no more than **three clans** may cluster within that radius. Sister-clanning (multiple clans acting as one indivisible group to bypass limits) is prohibited; IC vassalage may be allowed without evading spacing rules.\n- Clan warps must be placed at least **1/2 map grid** from base locations and need the applicable staff assistance. Protected-zone buffer rules still apply.\n- Inactivity: a member who has not logged in for **3 weeks** is removed from the clan under SOLACE's chosen replacement for the former two-week deletion. Inactive members do not count for inflation of building/decoration allowances in audits; notify staff via ticket for absence.\n\n## Building caps\nInherited base caps and maximum extensions, chosen by clan membership. Extension allowance may come from qualifying gameplay research and **donation building extension** as approved by the owner. These caps are ceilings, not automatic free building pieces. [CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH: donation availability and current Funcom/server monetization permissions before accepting payments.]\n\n| Members | Base pieces | Base placeables | Max extra pieces | Max extra placeables | Absolute max pieces | Absolute max placeables |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 280 | 160 | 50 | 20 | 330 | 180 |\n| 2 | 520 | 220 | 70 | 40 | 590 | 260 |\n| 3 | 760 | 280 | 100 | 60 | 860 | 340 |\n| 4 | 1,000 | 340 | 125 | 80 | 1,125 | 420 |\n| 5 | 1,240 | 400 | 150 | 100 | 1,365 | 500 |\n| 6 | 1,450 | 455 | 350 | 100 | 1,700 | 555 |\n| 7 | 1,660 | 510 | 350 | 120 | 2,010 | 630 |\n| 8 | 1,870 | 565 | 350 | 120 | 2,220 | 685 |\n| 9 | 2,080 | 620 | 500 | 150 | 2,580 | 770 |\n| 10 | 2,260 | 670 | 500 | 150 | 2,760 | 820 |\n| 11 | 2,400 | 710 | 500 | 150 | 2,900 | 860 |\n| 12 | 2,600 | 750 | 500 | 150 | 3,100 | 900 |\n\n**Legacy figures reproduced numerically for owner's adopted policy; game mod implementation must be verified.** Inherited in-game Masonry research can grant an extension up to the same ceilings. Research extensions do not stack with each other; explicitly identified donation allowances can follow their published exception.\n\n## Mount and decorative NPC allowances\nMaximum **one mount per player**, with a clan cap of **three**. Flaggis and wallpapers need staff ticket approval and should remain under the admin-controlled placement workflow. Limits:\n\n| Active clan size | Flaggis | Wallpapers |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1–4 | 3 | 1 |\n| 5–8 | 6 | 2 |\n| 9–12 | 9 | 3 |\n\nOne **Thespian per clan**, only in the **Hub Player Market**. Turn off head tracking; use vanilla armour only and no accessories where this applies to your installed NPC mod. No NPC as unraidable gold/item storage, and no trading of items intended to be non-droppable.\n\n## Storage restrictions\nThe legacy rule limits inventories for performance. Do not use decorative containers as hidden storage. Inherited personal inventory cap is **30 slots excluding the action bar**, subject to actual deployed mod configuration and approved in-world expansion. A standard personal storage chest has **25 slots**; an improved version through Masonry has **40**. The legacy per-base inventory caps are:\n\n| Per clan | Allowed |\n|---|---:|\n| Vault | 1 |\n| Donator Vault | 1 (only if legally/technically enabled) |\n| Dismantling Bench | 1 |\n| Freezer | 1 |\n| Universal Furnace | 1 |\n| Universal Crafting Station | 1 |\n| Processing Station | 1 |\n\n| Per player | Allowed |\n|---|---:|\n| Personal Chest | 1 |\n| One Elixir Cabinet, Jewellery Box **or** Magical Lockbox | 1 |\n\nInactive junk can be cleaned by scheduled server scripts, if deployed; staff should publish what those scripts delete. Deleted junk generally isn't refundable under inherited rules.\n\n## Restricted locations\n**No fictional coordinates are published.** Special utility sites often reserve a **1/2-grid** perimeter; principal public market/arena-like sites a **3/4-grid** perimeter. A SOLACE restricted-map overlay will be published after the map is confirmed. All instanced dungeons remain no-build zones.\n","09-hub":"# The Hub\n*Come to trade, work, meet people, or discover what a city does to troublemakers.*\n\n## What belongs here\nThe Hub is SOLACE's shared civic centre. **Player-operated markets and permitted Thespians exist here only.** It is where profession work, shops and everyday RP take place. It is not a zone where characters are OOC or universally safe.\n\n## Hub PvP: read before attacking\n<CRITICAL PUBLIC WARNING, style as visible fixed alert>\n**PvP is allowed inside the Hub. Raids and sieges against the Hub are not allowed.** The character who starts the attack accepts special consequences:\n\n**If the attacker wins:** Regular RP/combat rules apply to the encounter, but the attacker may give the victim **Injury only**. The attacker **cannot rob or kidnap** the person they attacked in the Hub.\n\n**If the attacker loses:** The defeated attacker falls under the **No Value of Life (NVL)** rule for initiating violence in town. The person they attacked may **kill them**, **take them as a slave**, or have them **jailed in the Hub**. Enslavement still follows the consent rules on `/rules/consequences`; if the attacker does not consent to enslavement, jail in the Hub is the alternative. Staff must verify who initiated and log the outcome for dispute review.\n\n**No exploiting town protections:** Hub protection is not a tool to stage attacks and hide. The Hub replaces the old rule permitting a four-person city raid; **Hub raids are forbidden**.\n\n## Hub services\n- Player Market: trading and merchant NPCs under one-Thespian-per-clan policy.\n- Blacksmith sourcing: the special **Feast Ring** is offered at the Hub vendor for **1 Gold** (durability applies).\n- Profession work: City Guard Duty (Fighter, Slaver, Thief) and Tavern Work (all other professions), each a 1-hour shift with RP, plus paid healing by Medics. Rewards are on `/economy`.\n- Shared social space: quiet RP, events and a meeting ground for characters of different backgrounds.\n\n## Example\nOne character chooses to initiate PvP against a patron in the Hub. The attacker wins. They may apply an injury, but not robbery or capture. If the attacker instead loses, the NVL rule applies to **the attacker**: the patron may kill them, take them as a slave, or have them jailed in the Hub.\n","10-professions":"# Professions\n*What does your character bring to the table?*\n\nEvery profession grants **+2 to two RPR skills** and has a long-term **Mastery** reward. Ability rolls use **1d20 + skill**; see `/rpr` for the full dice system.\n\nProfessions are a character's everyday specialty: a reason to meet others, offer a service, find employment and create RP. They are **not** the advanced progression tracks called Classes. Every character picks a Profession, including characters who also hold a Class. SOLACE has **eight professions**. Each profession page lists every skill with its rules, limits and an example.\n\n| Profession | In one sentence | Skills | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bard** | A performer who changes the mood of a room. | Performance, Inspire and Charm. | Confirmed. |\n| **Bounty Hunter** | A professional tracker of people and leads. | Tracking, Read Lies and Bounty Contract. | Confirmed. |\n| **Medic** | Someone you want beside you after the fight. | Treat Injury, Faster Recovery and Revitalize. | Confirmed. |\n| **Fighter** | A character trained to endure physical conflict. | Endurance, Hard to Break and Battle Ready. | Confirmed. |\n| **Thief** | Finds a way through doors and around trust. | Lockpicking, Theft, Deception and Liar’s Perfume. | Confirmed. |\n| **Alchemist** | Turns ingredients into consequences. | Brewing six elixirs: Truth, Oblivion, Babbling, Submission, Restoration and Desire. | Confirmed. |\n| **Slaver** | A captor specializing in agreed enslavement RP. | Break Will, Truth Compulsion and Intimidation. | Confirmed. |\n| **Courtier** | A schemer and dealmaker who wins with words, letters and bargains. | Silver Tongue, Subterfuge and Merchant. | Confirmed. |\n\n## Bard\nA tavern needs more than tables. Bards create performances, celebrations, rumours and social scenes. Their performance can calm a crowd, lift spirits with healing or win someone over, but it never takes away another player's choice.\n\n## Bounty Hunter\nA professional tracker who follows RP trails from POIs, forces the truth out of suspects and can hunt down characters who have piled up serious PK reasons. Tracking goes through a ticket; it never reveals an exact location.\n\n## Medic\nHelps injured characters return to the world. Medics treat wounds after a fight, speed up recovery and restore a tired patient's strength. The people everyone wants nearby after a bad night.\n\n## Fighter\nA resilient frontline character. Fighters don't hit harder; they last longer and take less lasting harm from a lost fight.\n\n## Thief\nA Thief opens locks with a lockpick item, steals within the robbery table limits and hides behind an extra /act name. Every break-in leaves a **POI**, and at least one member of the targeted clan must be online. Their Liar’s Perfume can make everyone nearby believe a single command.\n\n## Alchemist\nThe Alchemist creates special potions with powerful temporary effects. Each potion can be crafted once per day, needs no dice roll and is a physical item that can be stored, traded or sold.\n\n## Slaver\nA captor who specializes in agreed enslavement RP. The Slaver breaks a consenting captive's will over time, compels the truth and frightens people into keeping their distance. Captivity rules are server rules for everyone; see `/rules/consequences`.\n\n## Courtier\nCourtiers are skilled in diplomacy, persuasion, political maneuvering, forgery, intrigue and trade. They are most effective in social situations where information, reputation and influence matter more than brute force. They also know how to bargain for a better price. A forged letter only works if the Courtier knows the character they imitate well enough to make it believable.\n\n\n## Planned daily profession activity: not yet launched\nThe team discussed paid-for-by-game-currency shift RP around the Hub: Bard at tavern, Medic at treatment centre, Fighter/Bounty Hunter on city watch, Alchemist at shop, and Thief in tavern-related assignments, with a roughly one-hour RP shift concept. **This is meeting ideation, not a requirement or an extra confirmed reward beyond 10 Silver daily and 1 Gold weekly.**\n\n### How to choose\nPick the profession that starts scenes you will enjoy. A social character might be a Bard, Medic or Courtier; an investigative character a Bounty Hunter or Thief; someone who likes making and trading items an Alchemist or Courtier. Staff will publish switching policies, cooldowns and application limits before deployment. See `/classes` for Sorcerer, Blacksmith and Wise.\n","11-classes":"# Classes\n*Specializations you develop through play.*\n\nEvery class grants **+2 to two RPR skills**. Class abilities that need a roll use **1d20 + skill**; see `/rpr` for the full dice system.\n\nClasses are different from Professions. They open through applications, quests and mechanics rather than simply describing a character's everyday work. **Three classes are planned: Sorcerer, Blacksmith and Wise.** A character with a Class must also choose a Profession. Mechanical PvP stays mechanical; custom class checks are narrative/specialist tools and cannot replace combat results.\n\n# Sorcerer\n*Knowledge has a price. Progress is earned through blood rites.*\n\nThe Sorcerer is a lore-conscious custom class requiring an application and IC ritual development. The meeting favored five levels with a **fresh blood requirement at each new stage**, rather than a cumulative bank. It also explored each ability below.\n\n| Tier | Blood requirement | Unlocked power | What it does |\n|---:|---|---|---|\n| I | 1 character's blood | **Intent Reading** | Sense broadly positive/negative intent directed at the Sorcerer. |\n| II | 2 characters' blood | **Mind Control** | The target carries out one single command. |\n| III | 3 characters' blood | **Memory Erasure** | Affect a particular target's memory of an incident, not what others know. |\n| IV | 4 characters' blood | **Invisibility** | **30 minutes** of limited invisibility. |\n| V | 5 characters' blood | **Empowerment** | An ultimate buff for self or one nearby character. |\n\n### Empowerment: meeting's unfinalized candidate\nA **2-hour** buff once per day was discussed, with approximate **+5% Strength**, **+5% Agility**, **+20 Stamina** and **+20 Health**. Transcript uncertainty around STR notation and stacking makes these **not live balance values**. Sorcery branches such as Necromancer, Demonologist, Shaman, Hexer and Diviner were floated as concepts, not approved subclasses. No automatic first-contact PK right is granted to Bounty Hunters based on suspected sorcery; this was only debated. Ritual proof, blood sourcing, cooldown, staff ticket and opt-outs all require implementation specifications.\n\n# Blacksmith\n*The person who keeps rare equipment in circulation.*\n\n\nThe Blacksmith crafts legendary fittings and the Feast Ring. No dice roll is needed; required materials are shown in-game. Every item sells for **1 Gold** at the Hub market.\n\n| Item | Effect | Cooldown |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Legendary Weapon Fitting** | Increases Weapon Damage and Armor Penetration. | 2 days |\n| **Legendary Spike Weapon Fitting** | Increases Armor Penetration. | 2 days |\n| **Legendary Armor Fitting** | Increases Armor Points. | 2 days |\n| **Feast Ring** | Carry up to 1,000 Feast items with no weight. 1,000 uses, then it breaks. | 1 week |\n\n# Wise\n*Faith, knowledge and divine ritual.*\n\nThe Wise are scholars, spiritual leaders, priests, mystics and keepers of divine knowledge. Unlike Sorcerers, who gain power through forbidden practices, blood rituals and manipulation, the Wise gain their abilities through faith, knowledge, worship and divine ritual.\n\nA Wise character must follow the lore and religious practices of the deity they worship. A ritual dedicated to Mitra should not look the same as a ritual dedicated to Set, Ymir, Derketo or another deity. Each ritual must reflect the beliefs, traditions, offerings, prayers and practices of that god.\n\n### Wise ritual rules\nEvery new Wise level needs its own ritual. No blood is required.\n- A ticket must be opened before the ritual. The required ritual materials are shared in the ticket.\n- The ritual must be lore-appropriate for the Wise's deity.\n- The ritual RP must be recorded and sent to staff through the ticket.\n- The required number of worshippers must take part.\n- Once the ritual is approved, the related skill unlocks.\n\n## Class application\nClasses are special applications. You must request the Class in a ticket and clearly describe the kind of RP you want to do with it.\n\n**A character with a Class must also choose a Profession.**\n","12-economy-and-quests":"# Economy, Crafting & Quests\n*A coin is more interesting when it changes hands.*\n\n## Daily & Weekly Quests\n| Quest | Reward |\n|---|---|\n| **Daily Quests (2)** | **10 Silver total** |\n| **Weekly Quest** | **100 Silver or 1 Gold** |\n\n### Daily Quests\nThere are two daily quests. Together they give **10 Silver**.\n\n| Daily quest | Requirement | Reward |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Hub Duty** | Work a 1-hour Profession Work shift in the Hub (City Guard Duty or Tavern Work) and roleplay during it. | 5 Silver |\n| **Shard Hunt** | Collect 5 Shards by defeating the 5 special bosses. | 5 Silver |\n\n### Weekly Quest requirement\nThe Weekly Quest requires the player to collect **30 Shards**.\n- Shards are obtained by defeating the **5 special bosses** located around the map.\n- Players may repeatedly hunt these bosses until they have collected the required 30 Shards.\n\n## Profession Work\nProfession work gives characters a way to earn money through active roleplay inside the Hub. This is the **Hub Duty** daily quest: a 1-hour shift with RP earns **5 Silver**.\n\n### City Guard Duty\nThe following professions may take City Guard Duty:\n- Fighter\n- Slaver\n- Thief\n\nDuring the shift, they patrol the Hub for 1 hour and are paid for protecting the city.\n\n### Tavern Work\nAll other professions may work in the Hub Tavern:\n- Bard\n- Bounty Hunter\n- Medic\n- Alchemist\n- Courtier\n\nDuring the shift, they help out the tavern keeper and are free to roleplay however they like. The shift must last **1 hour**.\n\n### Medic Work\nMedics may earn money by offering healing services through RP, as well as through Tavern Work.\n\nBefore starting treatment, the Medic must clearly state the price of the service to the patient.\n- The price must be agreed, or at least clearly stated, before the healing RP begins.\n- Once the treatment has been completed, the Medic may not introduce a new price afterward.\n- A Medic cannot finish the healing first and then demand payment that was never mentioned beforehand.\n\nInside the Medic building, Medics may advertise their availability with an IC announcement such as *\"A healer is available.\"* or *\"I am a healer and I am now taking patients.\"*\n\n## Hub Market\nThe Hub sells several special items directly.\n\n| Item | Effect | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Amulet of Solace** | +15 Strength, +15 Agility | 10 Gold |\n| **Talisman of Solace** | +40 Health, +40 Stamina | 10 Gold |\n| **Feast Ring** | Use/carry up to 1,000 Feast items without weight burden. Breaks after 1,000 uses. | 1 Gold |\n| **Legendary Weapon Fitting** | Increases Weapon Damage and Armor Penetration. | 1 Gold |\n| **Legendary Spike Weapon Fitting** | Increases Armor Penetration. | 1 Gold |\n| **Legendary Armor Fitting** | Increases Armor Points. | 1 Gold |\n\nAll player markets belong in the **Hub**. Market Thespians are limited to **one per clan**, and cannot be used as invulnerable banks or forbidden-item exchanges. Social trade can still take place between characters, but permanent player market placements are Hub-only.\n\n### Feast Ring\nThe Feast Ring allows its wearer to use up to 1,000 Feast items without carrying their normal weight.\n- **Durability:** 1,000 uses. After 1,000 uses, the ring breaks.\n- **Hub price:** 1 Gold\n- Can also be crafted by a Blacksmith.\n\n### Legendary Weapon Fitting\nA high-grade fitting designed to increase a weapon's overall offensive power.\n- Increased Weapon Damage\n- Increased Armor Penetration\n- **Hub price:** 1 Gold\n\n### Legendary Spike Weapon Fitting\nA specialized fitting designed to improve a weapon's ability to penetrate armor.\n- Increased Armor Penetration\n- **Hub price:** 1 Gold\n\n### Legendary Armor Fitting\nA reinforced fitting designed to increase the defensive value of armor.\n- Increased Armor Points\n- **Hub price:** 1 Gold\n\n### Amulet of Solace\nA powerful Hub-exclusive accessory.\n- +15 Strength\n- +15 Agility\n- **Hub price:** 10 Gold\n\n### Talisman of Solace\nA powerful Hub-exclusive accessory focused on survivability.\n- +40 Health\n- +40 Stamina\n- **Hub price:** 10 Gold\n\n## Farming philosophy\nRoutine Conan material farming should leave enough time for character-driven RP. The meetings discussed easier access to early build resources. This is a direction, **not** a promised server multiplier or a promise of endless free resources.\n","13-races-and-relations":"# Peoples & Cultures of the Hyborian World\n*Your birthplace gives you a history, not a mandatory personality.*\n\nSOLACE is based on Conan lore. In Conan, many options commonly called 'races' in game menus are better described as peoples, realms or cultural backgrounds. Do not assume a person's background decides every alliance or that a historical feud gives you permission to KOS someone. Any custom racial stat bonuses, application restrictions, exceptional species, culture-specific abilities or quotas must be published separately before they exist.\n\n## Choose a background\nThese are brief writing prompts, not exhaustive cultural laws, and each culture can support many character types.\n\n| People/culture | Starting point for your character | Interesting RP hooks |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Aquilonian** | Western Hyborian kingdom with nobility, soldiers and frontier politics. | Soldier, courtier, settler, critic of the crown. |\n| **Nemedian** | Powerful Hyborian kingdom with scholarly and religious traditions. | Archivist, diplomat, rival noble, explorer. |\n| **Cimmerian** | Rugged highland clans north of Aquilonia; Conan's people. | Hunter, warrior, clan exile, wanderer. |\n| **Nordheimer** | Northern **Aesir** and **Vanir** peoples, with distinct loyalties and traditions. | Raider, skald, seafarer, mercenary. |\n| **Hyperborean** | Cold eastern/northern kingdom, known in stories for stern power structures. | Escapee, soldier, traveller, political dissident. |\n| **Pict** | Tribal peoples of the western wilderness with longstanding frontier conflicts. | Scout, ritualist, trader, clan representative. |\n| **Shemite** | Diverse Shemitish cities, pastoral communities and desert traditions. | Merchant, caravan guard, performer, nomad. |\n| **Stygian** | Ancient southern kingdom associated with mystery, temples and the Styx. | Scholar, sorcery seeker, soldier, exile. |\n| **Darfari** | A people of Darfar, south of Stygia; Conan fiction features distinctive religious/tribal groups. | Traveller, outsider, rebel, devotee; avoid reducing a person to an NPC enemy caricature. |\n| **Kushite** | Southern peoples from Kush and neighboring regions. | Sailor, artisan, warrior, emissary. |\n| **Zamorian** | Eastern urban cultures, frequently associated in stories with trade and intrigue. | Trader, thief, court agent, exile. |\n| **Zingaran** | Western maritime kingdom with political rivals and seafaring interests. | Sailor, corsair, merchant, noble. |\n| **Argossean** | Port-city and coastal commercial culture. | Shipmaster, broker, harbor worker. |\n| **Hyrkanian** | Horse-oriented steppe and eastern traditions. | Rider, scout, caravan escort. |\n| **Turanian** | Eastern imperial culture associated with military expansion and wealthy cities. | Officer, trader, courier. |\n| **Khitan** | Far-eastern kingdom/cultural sphere with distant philosophies and arts. | Wanderer, artisan, scholar. |\n| **Vendhyan** | Far-eastern/southern courtly and regional traditions. | Envoy, guard, healer, exile. |\n| **Himelian** | Mountain societies of the eastern highlands. | Guide, scout, herder. |\n| **Yamatai** | Eastern-inspired culture present in Conan Exiles's expanded cosmetic setting. | Swordsperson, craftsperson, distant traveller. |\n| **Hyborian (general)** | A broad cultural ancestry, not one single automatic kingdom identity. | Choose a more specific city, polity or frontier background where useful. |\n| **Other Conan backgrounds** | Kambujan, Khari, tribal/region-specific characters and other lore-consistent origins. | Ask the lore team when a less common option needs clarification. |\n\n**Availability warning:** Listing a people here is a lore guide, not an automatic confirmation that every cosmetic pack, mod race, supernatural identity or homebrew ability is playable at launch. The final playable list must match the actual character-creation implementation.\n\n## Historical relationships: a starting point for RP\n**Legend:** `Rivalry/Border conflict` = historical state/tribal tension; `Raids/hostility` = recurring conflict in published source material; `Trade/complex` = contact without a single permanent alignment; `Internal differences` = a grouped category contains rival subgroups. **None is an automatic character-specific enemy tag, combat permission, racial bonus, or fixed alliance.** Canon chronology varies, and SOLACE has not settled an exact lore year.\n\n| Pair / grouping | Typical historical tension or relationship | Why an encounter might matter | Gameplay status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Aquilonia ↔ Nemedia | Rival great Hyborian powers; political and military competition. | Border officer meets a Nemedian merchant or envoy. | Historical context, **not** automatic hostility. |\n| Aquilonia ↔ Pictish frontier groups | Frontier conflict and raiding are recurring Conan themes. | Patrol, captive exchange, illicit border trade. | Historical context, **not** KOS. |\n| Aquilonia ↔ Cimmerian clans | Northern frontier contact, raids and attempted expansion create distrust. | Soldier and highlander disagree over a frontier claim. | Character choice decides the response. |\n| Cimmerians ↔ Picts | Long mythic/historical antagonism in Hyborian history. | Old oral tradition colors a new meeting. | No inherited personal blood feud by default. |\n| Aesir ↔ Vanir | Distinct Nordheimer groups often depicted in mutual conflict. | Competing northern warbands or unexpected cooperation. | Internal northern rivalry, not universal enmity. |\n| Nordheimer ↔ Cimmerian clans | Raids and border contact recur in northern tales. | Shared survival against a third faction. | Situation-dependent. |\n| Stygia ↔ Shemitish peoples | Long history of domination, trade, power struggles and shifting independence. | Priest, trader and runaway meet in exile. | Historical context, not a forced relationship. |\n| Stygia ↔ Darfari/other southern neighbors | Cross-border coercion and slaving appear in Conan's world. | A former captive seeks allies or a new life. | This is a state/history prompt, never consent to enslavement. |\n| Aquilonia ↔ Hyperborea | Episodes of hostility in Hyborian geopolitical history. | Rival claimants meet far from home. | Era-sensitive, not permanent faction war. |\n| Zingara ↔ Argos | Neighboring maritime commerce and competition. | Merchant/corsair rivalry at a neutral market. | RP hook rather than declared war. |\n| Hyrkanian/Turanian powers ↔ western kingdoms | Contact and expansion change dramatically across the Hyborian chronology. | Courier, scout or displaced noble. | Requires chosen setting year. |\n\n### How to use this table\nPlay a believable personal history. A Cimmerian and an Aquilonian may be old enemies, comrades, lovers or strangers. An inherited grievance can start a scene, but only IC actions and actual approved combat rules can escalate it. Do not use a website culture table as a metagaming hit list.\n\n[Read expanded culture dossiers →](/races/cultures)\n\n## Character application prompts\nWhere were you born? Who raised you? What does your character believe about home? Which language, faith or profession matters to them? What is one stereotype they fit and one they don't? Why did exile change their plans? How much of their homeland's politics do they actually know?\n\n## Sources and limits\nThis overview uses the owner-requested Conan basis, examples from Robert E. Howard's *The Hyborian Age*, and the Conan Exiles Wiki's cultural category. It is a short **editorial interpretation**, not a claimed official playable roster or a binding alignment chart. Reference links and verification notes live in `reference/LORE_SOURCES.md`.\n","14-support-and-moderation":"# Help, Tickets & Moderation\n*Ask a question. Report a problem. Know what happens next.*\n\n## Open the right ticket\n| Ticket | Use it for | Who should review |\n|---|---|---|\n| **General Question** | Basic rules, joining, clarification. | Available support staff. |\n| **Developer Ticket** | Bugs, mods, server issues, lost data evidence. | Technical team. |\n| **Dispute Ticket** | PvP, metagaming, consequential rule disagreement. | Independent conflict reviewers. |\n| **Staff Report** | Complaints about staff conduct. | Someone not involved, with restricted access. |\n| **Raid Ticket** | Raid approval, objective, online evidence and scheduling. | Independent raid observer. |\n| **Store Application / Store Ticket** | Hub market/shop placement requests. | Economy/building team. |\n| **Permadeath Request** | Proposed standard PK/PD and exceptional cases. | Restricted admin review without implicated staff. |\n| **Character / Lore Ticket** | Concept, approved appearance, rare background, reroll/shelving. | Whitelist/lore team. |\n| **Consent/Safety Ticket** | Boundary concern or immediate sensitive-content problem. | Appropriate restricted reviewer. |\n\n**Ticket channels/roles are proposed operational names from the meetings, not confirmed Discord links.** [Insert real support URL and assign access permissions before publication.]\n\n## A ticket does not automatically pause RP\nWhere the situation is safe to continue, the live RP scene proceeds while staff reviews a ticket. A proven error can lead to a narrowly documented correction or retcon later. Staff may pause an active scene or take temporary protective action where player safety, serious exploitation or irreversible consequences require it.\n\n## Evidence and outcomes\nInclude date/time, character names, rule section, screenshots/recordings, unedited context and what remedy you request. **Recordings are for confidential ticket evidence, not IC discovery or public drama.** The person whose character/faction is involved must step away from adjudicating that incident. Final action comes from a human staff member; AI may assist with drafting/organization but does not substitute for evidence.\n\n## Possible responses\nClarification, warning, documented strike, time-limited suspension, permanent ban or immediate proportionate safety intervention. Reasons and an appeal path should be stated. A report is not itself proof; equally, the existence of a rule loophole does not immunize bad-faith abuse. Staff conduct is reportable.\n\n## What to expect\n1. Ticket filed and categorized.\n2. Reviewer checks their neutrality/possible conflict of interest.\n3. Evidence and relevant rule version collected.\n4. Impact, disputed facts and any protective measure recorded.\n5. Decision with stated findings and any corrective action.\n6. Appeal to someone uninvolved where available.\n\n**Do not invent exact SLA response hours, moderators or a punishment strike ladder until the staff team approves them.**\n","15-faq":"# Frequently Asked Questions\n\n**What kind of server is SOLACE?** 21+ English-language Conan Exiles roleplay with PvP and PvE, an emphasis on player-written stories, social RP and lasting IC consequences.\n\n**Is the Hub safe?** It cannot be raided/sieged, but **PvP is allowed**. A victorious attacker may only injure the target. An attacker who loses falls under NVL: the person they attacked may kill them, take them as a slave, or have them jailed in the Hub if they refuse enslavement. Read `/hub`.\n\n**Do you use dice to settle fights?** No. Mechanical PvP is the default. Specialist RP abilities and appropriate perception/stealth rolls are separate from dice combat.\n\n**Can my friend join a fight after it starts?** No. Narrow exception: the assaulted character reaches their **own base**, and people **already inside** may defend them.\n\n**How do I start PvP?** Intent emote, approved PvP intent command, everyone initially in range declares Join/Surrender and Ready, then a 10-second start timer. See `/rules/pvp`.\n\n**Are raids offline?** No. A qualifying fraction of an active defending clan must be online, a ticket is required and an independent staff member supervises.\n\n**How long may a character be captive?** Captivity lasts **24 hours** for every character, and active captors owe the captive **2 hours of real RP** within it, or the captive is free to leave. Longer-term captivity is allowed when both players agree. Everything happens with consent. See `/rules/consequences`.\n\n**What is Broken?** The Slaver ability has three successful, consensual Breaking stages on the same target. Its full effects are still in development. No roll replaces player consent.\n\n**What are the professions?** Bard, Bounty Hunter, Medic, Fighter, Thief, Alchemist and Slaver. See `/professions`.\n\n**What are the classes?** Sorcerer, Blacksmith and Wise. Each class page lists its abilities level by level. See `/classes`.\n\n**What is the daily/weekly reward?** **10 Silver daily**, **1 Gold weekly**.\n\n**How much is a Feast Ring?** **1 Gold at the Hub.** It has durability. A Blacksmith may craft **one per week**.\n\n**Can I run a market at my base?** Permanent player markets and Market Thespians are Hub-only. Social trade elsewhere isn't an excuse to place a forbidden secondary shop/NPC.\n\n**May I build a second base?** No permanent second base. Small temporary RP camps may be removed after use or extended by permission.\n\n**Can I pay for a higher building limit?** Donation extension was retained as a desired server policy, subject to lawful/platform-permitted implementation. No live product/pricing is published yet.\n\n**When do inactive clan members get removed?** **Three weeks** under the SOLACE amendment; warn staff by ticket if you plan to be away.\n\n**When can I unshelf a living character?** **30 days** after shelving, subject to current conflict/character process.\n\n**Can I use a recording to locate another character?** No, that is metagaming. Evidence stays in tickets; selected promotional clips can be shared only under privacy/content rules.\n\n**Must my culture hate its traditional rival?** No. The lore relationship chart provides historical RP prompts, never forced hostility or KOS rights.\n\n**Is a ticket an automatic RP freeze?** No. Staff can pause an exceptional unsafe/irreversible scene and can review later for a correction.\n\n**Where do I appeal a staff decision?** Use the appropriate appeal/report route listed under `/support` once Discord ticket links are activated.\n","16-updates":"# News & Rule Changes\n## Draft v0.1: 30 September 2026\nSOLACE's first website content pack combines the adopted mechanical baseline with approved SOLACE decisions and the September planning meetings. **It is a drafting package, not a claim that hosting, mods, application forms or the final rulebook have launched.**\n\n### Confirmed decisions documented here\n- Eight professions (Courtier added); three classes (Wise added).\n- Mechanical PvP; new no-late-join rule with a narrow home-base defense exception.\n- Hub permits PvP but not raids; an initiating attacker who loses falls under NVL (the victim may kill, enslave or jail them in the Hub).\n- 24-hour captivity with two hours' required active captor RP; consent form to be published.\n- Three-week clan inactivity threshold; 30-day living-character unshelving.\n- 10 Silver daily / 1 Gold weekly.\n- Feast Ring durability, 1 Gold Hub price, one Blacksmith craft per week.\n- Conan lore; original building caps adopted, player markets restricted to Hub.\n\n### Before publication\nResolve pending fields in `reference/OPEN_DECISIONS.md`, run content review and technical verification, then publish a dated rule revision with staff/owner sign-off. Changes must state their effective date, whether they affect ongoing scenes, and the appeal/exception process.\n","17-legal-and-privacy":"# Privacy, Recording & Sharing\n*Keep the memory. Protect the people in it.*\n\n## The baseline\nDo not record/stream a current RP scene to gather IC information unavailable to your character. Do not use another person's stream, screenshots or a recording to hunt them, follow secret negotiations or rally OOC allies. This is metagaming even when the media was posted publicly elsewhere.\n\n## Confidential evidence\nRecordings and screenshots may be submitted to staff when relevant to a rule violation or exploit. Keep them inside the ticket and do not distribute them to players who were not involved. Avoid selective editing that hides important context; mark time stamps where possible.\n\n## Approved community promotion\nSOLACE may allow screenshots, polished highlights, event footage and cinematic promotional media that depict **consenting participants** and do not expose restricted scenes or create IC advantage. Agree to publication with the people identifiable in a recording before posting it. When in doubt, request a content-sharing review ticket. Prior-season footage does not automatically waive a person's privacy.\n\n## Sensitive content\nNever post explicit personal/sexual scenes, personal information, staff tickets, private Discord conversation content or identifying details without appropriate permission. Avoid doxxing and unwanted contact. A consent form covers roleplay boundaries, not blanket rights to publicize material.\n\n## Website implementation notes\nPrivacy notice must accurately disclose the actual analytics, cookies, embedded Discord widgets, hosting and user forms once chosen. Do **not** invent GDPR claims, a company address, a retention period or data-contact email. Add a separate final legal policy before collecting personal data through the website.\n","18-reference-details":"# Reference Details & Edge Cases\n*The short pages explain what you need most often. This annex collects inherited edge-case mechanics and their exceptions so no one has to guess during a scene.*\n\n> **Release note:** This is a detailed inherited-rule annex, subject to successful implementation of the actual Conan mod setup. A source-specific item, racial feat or portal that SOLACE does not install must not be treated as available merely because the original reference mentions it. Owner-approved SOLACE overrides take precedence in case of conflict.\n\n## Post-combat specifics\n- A downed character is **Slightly Injured** at a minimum and stays at the down location while mechanical PvP is unresolved. Do not revive or carry the character out until fighting has ended, except for a permitted mechanical return to the exact location of the body.\n- After fighting, the winning side may permit aided movement. Players use a suitable aid/accept-aid emote, walk rather than run, and cannot warp until **three map tiles** from the original down point under the inherited rule.\n- If a new valid incident interrupts consequence processing, a person already downed can only surrender, not join or run. Any applicable unattended timer pauses during the interruption. This must **not** be exploited as a loophole to bring late allies into the original battle.\n- No unauthorised healing from outside the winning side during consequence processing. Moderate-or-higher injury blocks abilities/spells unless the explicit ability allows limited self-healing.\n- Only participants in the original legal encounter may give its consequences. You cannot hand a captured target to an uninvolved third party solely to deliver an otherwise unavailable consequence. A truly separate later event requires its own lawful initiation and reviewer scrutiny.\n\n## Injury and bodily consequence categories\n- **Major dismemberment:** removal of a limb or comparable permanent organ loss; source baseline says this is a **second-down** outcome and cannot naturally regenerate. Restoration requires a valid healing mechanic; the character's gear use must reflect loss (e.g. one-handed weapons after loss of arm/hand). Genital injury is sensitive content and requires specific OOC permission.\n- **Mutilation:** long-term scar/brand or loss of minor part, with Moderate Injury under the inherited scheme; special severe vision loss is treated as a later/second-down outcome. Inherited magical treatment may remove it only through a matching approved item/spell. Consent Form governs how far any lasting change may go.\n- **Robbery:** use exactly one lawful table choice for its category and obey the special crafted-item limits. A normal consequence is never blanket permission to loot buildings. A clue used for scrying may be emote-only, without taking a protected physical object.\n- **Spells:** the source's Primary/Secondary consequence spell design needs a published Conan-specific roster before it is functional.\n- **Permadeath:** normally a considered, administratively reviewed outcome. If it is permitted, it is the **only** consequence on that character. A major attack on a leader is not a free-kill pass on the entire settlement.\n- **Sexual assault content:** requires explicit, specific OOC agreement to participate in any sensitive theme, and refusal is sufficient. No prior IC offense creates automatic permission. No explicit scene is required by this website.\n\n## PvP intent edge cases\n- Initial observers in **local range** must declare their response at the start; this is different from bringing someone in once combat is underway.\n- Leaving an instance through its normal exit is permitted, but neither side may exploit loading screens or heal immediately at the doorway. Move **5 foundations** before fighting outside.\n- Source includes a Khari Dungeon-specific escape shortcut that counts as surrender. **Do not activate this rule unless the exact location exists on SOLACE's deployed map and the path has been tested.**\n- Flight is not an invulnerability loophole; if approved flight mechanics exist, land before relevant conflict.\n- Event KOS is only for explicitly announced, status-tagged activities; source used Lake Town Heist/Relic Hunting, **not current SOLACE event names**. Staff must publish the present event flag and player identification before enabling.\n\n## Raid edge cases\n- Thief lockpicking allows **at most two entrants** before a full approved raid is necessary; do not open additional doors for an entire unregistered army.\n- Raid objective may be broadly described but cannot be omitted.\n- Defenders may make the permitted home warp to protect their base; attackers do not gain comparable entry warp.\n- Attackers who fail to arrive from the declared location within **10 minutes** after the raid start timer may lose the raid and receive **24-hour** cooldown as a source administrative consequence.\n- A declared attempt ordinarily creates **3-day** target-group cooldown upon completion, with defender counter-action and defender-flight distinctions set out in `/rules/raids`.\n- Spectators who are not actually involved cannot arrive purely to watch OOC; allies require real IC communication rather than Discord mobilization.\n- Source requires music boxes off during raids, and prevents post-declaration building/dismantling/repair outside the identified siege-engine exception.\n\n## Looking for RP (LFRP), if the relevant mod is installed\n- Use a clear **Conflict/Hostile** tag where an LFRP advertisement is intended to lead to antagonistic roleplay (especially for Slaver scenarios).\n- Disable LFRP immediately if a scene becomes conflict or when another participant legitimately requests it; keep disabled through consequences/captivity.\n- Never use a live LFRP tag to locate someone's hidden base while approaching/exploring without consent.\n- Only an assigned Dungeon Master may apply a DM tag.\n\n## Character/account edge cases\n- Do not create a new character to pursue vengeance about your own previous character's death. No involvement in one's own old-character resurrection process.\n- A reroll contest must be about unresolved recent conflict and may be declined if there is no actual pursuit/engagement. Only approved reviewers may decide its merits.\n- Standard shelves retain character progression where technically possible; rare/special background entitlement from a retired ruleset is not automatically transferred.\n- Leaving Discord: open a notice ticket. A fake or alternate account used to evade bans may cause action against linked accounts where a knowingly involved participant helps evade enforcement.\n\n","19-culture-dossiers":"# Culture Dossiers\n*Practical guidance for making a Conan-rooted character. These are cultural snapshots, not inherited stats or personality tests.*\n\nThis page expands the quick `/races` table. **Nothing here automatically grants a combat modifier, predetermined faction, 'enemy' label, costume requirement or permission to attack.** Appearance is varied within every people and the setting's chronology is not locked yet.\n\n## Aquilonian\n**Region:** Western Hyborian kingdoms. **Background:** A realm with frontier armies, trade routes and competing noble interests. **RP traits to explore:** civic loyalty, court service, village pragmatism, life on contested borders. **Potential tensions:** Nemedia's competing power, Pictish frontiers, northern Cimmerian border history. **Possible opening:** An ex-soldier sells protection to a caravan whose owner is Nemedian.\n\n## Nemedian\n**Region:** Eastern neighbor and rival of Aquilonia. **Background:** Influential kingdom with notable learning, institutions and political ambitions. **RP traits to explore:** scholarship, diplomacy, soldiering, personal status. **Potential tensions:** Aquilonian geopolitical competition. **Opening:** A scholar seeks evidence of a ruined civilization without the patronage of home.\n\n## Cimmerian\n**Region:** Hard northern uplands. **Background:** Independent clans, rugged conditions, long contact and conflict with neighbors. **RP traits to explore:** kinship, practical survival, direct speech, distrust of conquest. None is mandatory. **Potential tensions:** Pictish historical feud, Aquilonian borders, Nordheimer raids. **Opening:** A wanderer has no interest in joining a northern war their relatives remember.\n\n## Aesir / Vanir (Nordheimer)\n**Region:** The northern lands of Asgard and Vanaheim. **Background:** Northern warrior and settlement traditions with differing tribal allegiances. **RP traits to explore:** oath-taking, sea or land travel, song, trade and family rivalries. **Potential tensions:** Aesir–Vanir rivalry; Cimmerian contact. **Opening:** A Vanir guard and an Aesir merchant reluctantly share watch.\n\n## Hyperborean\n**Region:** North/east of key Hyborian realms. **Background:** Severe northern climate and often oppressive political institutions in the stories. **RP traits to explore:** hierarchy, exile, duty, dissent, frontier livelihoods. **Potential tensions:** Aquilonian history and neighboring northern communities, according to era. **Opening:** A deserter wishes the word 'Hyperborean' did not answer every question about them.\n\n## Pict\n**Region:** Western wilderness/frontiers. **Background:** Varied tribal and spiritual traditions; stories often focus on contentious Aquilonian settlement frontiers. **RP traits to explore:** hunting, kinship, knowledge of terrain, diplomacy, protective community ties. **Potential tensions:** Aquilonian frontier and ancient Cimmerian myths. **Opening:** A scout has come to trade rather than fulfill someone else's expectation of a raid.\n\n## Shemite\n**Region:** Shem's cities, pastures and desert-adjacent communities. **Background:** Distinct communities with mercantile, pastoral and travelling traditions. **RP traits to explore:** poetry, commerce, navigation, mercenary work, spiritual life. **Potential tensions:** historical Stygian control and contact with nearby kingdoms. **Opening:** A caravan musician hopes to establish a permanent shop in the Hub.\n\n## Stygian\n**Region:** The kingdom south of the Styx. **Background:** Ancient institutions, temples, elite politics and sorcery in the fiction. **RP traits to explore:** ritual belief, archaeology, merchant wealth, military obligation, dissatisfaction with the state. **Potential tensions:** Shemitish history and exploitation of some southern peoples. **Opening:** A scholar rejects the assumptions others make about Stygian sorcery.\n\n## Darfari\n**Region:** Darfar, south of Stygia. **Background:** A fictional people represented through specific Conan tribal/NPC factions. **RP traits to explore:** family, migration, resistance, inherited ritual choices, ordinary survival; avoid treating every Darfari character as a single hostile NPC archetype. **Potential tensions:** Stygian exploitation in some source material. **Opening:** A traveller insists on being known for their deeds rather than a stranger's fear.\n\n## Kushite and southern neighbors\n**Region:** Kush and the wider southern lands. **Background:** Distinct cultures, routes and rulers in the Black Kingdoms. **RP traits to explore:** seafaring, settlement, defense, artisan work, diplomacy. **Potential tensions:** vary by polity and era; never infer a monolithic enemy or alliance. **Opening:** A craftsperson joins a mixed caravan and becomes its negotiator.\n\n## Zamorian\n**Region:** East of several central Hyborian realms. **Background:** Cities and mobile specialists; fiction often provides opportunities for urban intrigue. **RP traits to explore:** trade, theft, performance, craft, espionage. **Potential tensions:** specific city/clan disputes, not racial hatred. **Opening:** An expert lock worker is tired of every stranger calling them a thief.\n\n## Zingaran\n**Region:** Western coastal kingdom. **Background:** Maritime politics, commercial rivalry and sea travel. **RP traits to explore:** sailor, navigator, duelist, trader, harbor official. **Potential tensions:** Argossean maritime competition in settings that support it. **Opening:** A lost ship's captain looks for crew in the Hub.\n\n## Argossean\n**Region:** Coastal ports around Argos. **Background:** Trade and shipping connect coastal communities to wider politics. **RP traits to explore:** ship ownership, contracts, imports, tavern operations. **Potential tensions:** port competition or maritime feuds; resolve IC. **Opening:** A broker offers a route into markets blocked by war.\n\n## Hyrkanian / Turanian\n**Region:** Eastern steppe and, for Turan, its imperial/city centers. **Background:** Eastern horses, trade, war and shifting geopolitical horizons depending on chronology. **RP traits to explore:** riding, archery, messenger work, commercial ambition, soldiering. **Potential tensions:** western contact is chronologically dependent. **Opening:** A rider has crossed too many borders to believe a map tells the full story.\n\n## Khitan\n**Region:** Far-eastern lands. **Background:** Distant travel, specialist arts and distinct philosophical traditions in Conan's expanded world. **RP traits to explore:** crafts, scholarship, journeying, court service. **Potential tensions:** personal or faction-specific; no preassigned common foe. **Opening:** An artisan arrived seeking materials unavailable at home.\n\n## Vendhyan\n**Region:** Vendhya and neighboring eastern/southern realms. **Background:** Diverse regional political and courtly settings. **RP traits to explore:** emissary, guard, healer, pilgrim. **Potential tensions:** depend on the chosen exact origin. **Opening:** A former palace messenger would rather be anonymous.\n\n## Himelian\n**Region:** Eastern high mountain communities. **Background:** Travel, isolated passes and practical mountaineering. **RP traits to explore:** guide, fighter, hunter, courier. **Potential tensions:** local rivalries in specific mountain settings. **Opening:** A guide offers safe passage in exchange for news of home.\n\n## Yamatai / other expanded cosmetic backgrounds\n**Region:** Far eastern-inspired content represented in Conan Exiles cosmetics. **Background:** Always reconcile against the playable lore period and actual enabled content. **RP traits to explore:** craftsmanship, combat practice, long-distance exile. **Potential tensions:** unassigned by SOLACE. **Opening:** A stranger is asked to describe their route west.\n\n## Background application reminder\nWrite a person, not a census entry. Your character can oppose their homeland, reject a religion, serve another realm or start over entirely. Race/culture relations are for thoughtful RP and have **no mechanical enemy or PvP consequences on their own**.\n","20-rpr-system":"# Dice & RPR System\n\n*Roleplay Rolls, Profession Mastery & Class Ability Checks.*\n\n*SOLACE uses a lightweight d20 roleplay system for uncertain RP actions, Profession abilities, Class abilities, investigations and opposed roleplay actions. Mechanical PvP remains Conan Exiles mechanical combat and is not replaced by dice.*\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Core Rule\n\nMost RPR checks use:\n\n**1d20 + Final Skill Modifier**\n\nYour Final Skill Modifier is built from three possible sources:\n\n1. **Category Bonus**\n2. **Allocated Skill Points**\n3. **Profession / Class Bonus**\n\n### Character Creation\n\nEvery character receives:\n\n- **5 Category Points**\n- **35 Skill Points**\n\n### Category Point Rules\n\n- The 5 Category Points are distributed between the four main categories.\n- A single category may receive a maximum of **+3**.\n- Every point placed into a category gives **+1 to every skill inside that category**.\n\n### Skill Point Rules\n\n- The player distributes **35 Skill Points** between the 16 individual RPR skills.\n- A single skill may receive a maximum of **5 allocated Skill Points** during character creation.\n\n### Profession and Class Bonuses\n\n- Every Profession grants **+2 to two RPR skills** that represent its specialization.\n- Every Class grants **+2 to two RPR skills** that represent its specialization.\n- Profession and Class bonuses stack with Category and allocated Skill Points.\n- A skill's **final effective modifier can never exceed +10**.\n\n### Example\n\nA Courtier has:\n\n- Social +2\n- Persuasion +4 from allocated Skill Points\n- Courtier Profession Bonus: Persuasion +2\n\nTheir final Persuasion modifier is:\n\n**+8**\n\nIf Silver Tongue requires 16+, the player rolls:\n\n**1d20 + 8**\n\nA natural roll of 8 gives a final result of 16 and succeeds.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Four Main Categories\n\n### PHYSICAL\n\nPhysical represents bodily control, movement, coordination and direct physical action.\n\n#### Athletics\nUsed for raw physical effort.\n\nExamples:\n- Climbing a difficult surface.\n- Swimming through dangerous water.\n- Forcing open a stuck object.\n- Lifting or dragging something heavy.\n- Holding someone back through physical strength when the scene allows an RPR check.\n\n#### Acrobatics\nUsed for balance, controlled movement and difficult physical positioning.\n\nExamples:\n- Keeping balance on a narrow ledge.\n- Landing safely after a difficult jump.\n- Moving across unstable terrain.\n- Escaping a physical hold when the scene is being resolved through RPR rather than mechanical PvP.\n\n#### Sleight of Hand\nUsed for precise hand movements and subtle manual actions.\n\nExamples:\n- Picking a lock.\n- Concealing a small object.\n- Quietly moving or taking a small item during RP.\n- Performing a delicate hand-based trick.\n\n#### Stealth\nUsed to move, hide or remain unnoticed.\n\nExamples:\n- Moving quietly through a settlement.\n- Hiding from someone searching nearby.\n- Approaching a location without drawing attention.\n\n**Stealth does not create magical invisibility and does not override what another character could clearly see in game.**\n\n---\n\n### KNOWLEDGE\n\nKnowledge represents education, learned information, research and technical understanding.\n\n#### Arcana\nUsed for knowledge of sorcery, unnatural phenomena, rituals and supernatural signs.\n\nExamples:\n- Recognizing signs of sorcery.\n- Studying the remains of a ritual.\n- Understanding whether an occult symbol is meaningful.\n- Identifying unusual magical behavior when the character could reasonably know it.\n\n#### History\nUsed for historical and cultural knowledge.\n\nExamples:\n- Remembering an old war or ruler.\n- Recognizing a historical banner.\n- Knowing something about an ancient settlement.\n- Recalling important cultural events.\n\n#### Investigation\nUsed for deliberate, detailed examination and connecting evidence.\n\nExamples:\n- Examining a murder scene.\n- Searching a room for hidden clues.\n- Studying a damaged weapon to understand what happened.\n- Comparing documents or physical evidence.\n\nInvestigation is normally used when the character is **actively examining something**, while Perception is normally used to **notice something**.\n\n#### Religion\nUsed for gods, religious customs, sacred symbols and rituals.\n\nExamples:\n- Recognizing a religious symbol.\n- Understanding the purpose of a shrine.\n- Recalling the customs of a faith.\n- Performing or interpreting religious rites when appropriate.\n\n#### Medicine\nUsed for bodily injuries, illness, poison and medical understanding.\n\nExamples:\n- Examining a wound.\n- Determining whether someone was poisoned.\n- Understanding the likely cause of an injury.\n- Assessing whether a wounded person is stable.\n\nMedicine checks do not replace the special healing abilities of the Medic Profession.\n\n---\n\n### INSTINCT\n\nInstinct represents awareness, intuition, survival sense and reading the world around the character.\n\n#### Perception\nUsed to notice details through sight, hearing and general awareness.\n\nExamples:\n- Hearing movement nearby.\n- Spotting fresh blood on the ground.\n- Noticing someone attempting to hide.\n- Seeing a detail that is not automatically obvious.\n\n#### Insight\nUsed to read behavior, intent, emotional cues and inconsistencies.\n\nExamples:\n- Feeling that someone is hiding something.\n- Reading a person's mood.\n- Detecting suspicious behavior.\n- Opposing a Deception roll.\n\nA normal Insight check does **not** force another player to reveal the full truth. Special Profession or Class abilities may create stronger effects when their rules explicitly say so.\n\n#### Survival\nUsed for tracking, navigation and wilderness knowledge.\n\nExamples:\n- Following tracks.\n- Determining where a trail is heading.\n- Navigating through difficult terrain.\n- Recognizing signs that someone recently passed through an area.\n\n\n---\n\n### SOCIAL\n\nSocial represents communication, manipulation, pressure and performance.\n\n#### Persuasion\nUsed for honest persuasion, diplomacy and negotiation.\n\nExamples:\n- Convincing a guard to hear you out.\n- Negotiating a better agreement.\n- Trying to calm a disagreement through words.\n\nA normal Persuasion roll does not remove another player's agency. It helps resolve uncertain social RP but cannot force consent-based actions unless a specific Profession or Class ability explicitly allows an effect under its own rules.\n\n#### Deception\nUsed for lies, false stories, disguises and misleading information.\n\nExamples:\n- Lying about where you were.\n- Pretending to represent someone else.\n- Giving a believable false explanation.\n\nA common opposed check is:\n\n**Deception vs Insight**\n\n#### Intimidation\nUsed for threats, fear and social pressure.\n\nExamples:\n- Threatening someone into backing away.\n- Establishing a frightening presence.\n- Trying to make someone hesitate through fear.\n\nNormal Intimidation does not automatically force another player to obey. Profession abilities such as Slaver Intimidation use their own defined mechanical effect.\n\n#### Performance\nUsed for music, storytelling, acting, speeches and entertainment.\n\nExamples:\n- Playing music in a tavern.\n- Giving a public speech.\n- Telling a story to hold a crowd's attention.\n- Performing at an event.\n\n---\n\n## 3. General RP Checks\n\nRPR is not only for Profession or Class abilities. Any player may use the system when an uncertain RP action needs a fair resolution.\n\n### Standard Difficulty Guide\n\nStaff, event runners or the players involved may use the following difficulty guide:\n\n| Difficulty | Required Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Simple | **8+** |\n| Standard | **12+** |\n| Difficult | **16+** |\n| Extreme | **20+** |\n\nThe final result is always:\n\n**1d20 + Final Skill Modifier**\n\n#### Example: Investigation\n\nA player examines a body for details that are not immediately obvious.\n\nThe scene runner sets the check at **16**.\n\nThe character has Investigation +5.\n\nThey roll 13.\n\n**13 + 5 = 18, Success.**\n\nThe scene runner provides the clue that could reasonably be discovered.\n\n#### Example: Perception\n\nA player wants to notice whether someone recently passed through a dark alley.\n\nThe check is **12**.\n\nThe character has Perception +3 and rolls 7.\n\n**7 + 3 = 10, Failure.**\n\nThey do not notice anything reliable.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Opposed RP Checks\n\nWhen two characters are actively opposing each other, both may roll.\n\nThe higher final result wins.\n\nCommon examples:\n\n- **Deception vs Insight**\n- **Stealth vs Perception**\n- **Sleight of Hand vs Perception**\n- **Athletics vs Athletics**\n- **Athletics vs Acrobatics**, where appropriate\n\n#### Example: Lie vs Insight\n\nCharacter A tells a deliberate lie.\n\n- Character A rolls **1d20 + Deception**.\n- Character B rolls **1d20 + Insight**.\n\nCharacter A: 14 + 5 = **19**\n\nCharacter B: 12 + 4 = **16**\n\nCharacter A wins the opposed check.\n\nCharacter B does not gain mechanical confirmation that the statement is false.\n\n#### Tie\n\nIf an opposed check ends in a tie, the existing situation remains unchanged unless both players agree on another outcome.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RPR Quality Rule\n\nRPR exists to support roleplay, not replace it.\n\nA roll must be supported by an appropriate RP attempt.\n\nPlayers may not repeatedly make one-line emotes, spam rolls or arrange empty scenes only to gain progression, Profession Mastery or mechanical advantages.\n\nQualifying RP should be:\n\n- Properly roleplayed.\n- Appropriate to the character and situation.\n- Given enough time and effort to create an actual scene.\n- Supported by believable context.\n- Meaningful enough to justify the requested result.\n\nStaff may reject progression evidence that exists only to farm counters or rewards.\n\n**Progression requirements are story milestones, not achievement farming.**\n\n---\n\n## 6. Profession & Class Rolls\nEvery Profession and Class page lists its starting RPR bonuses, the skill and target number for each ability, and its Mastery reward. See `/professions` and `/classes`, or the quick references below.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Quick Reference: Profession Ability Difficulties\n\n| Profession | Ability | RPR Skill | Required Result |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| Bard | Performance | Performance | **16+** |\n| Bard | Charm | Persuasion | **16+** |\n| Bounty Hunter | Tracking | Survival | **12–15 partial / 16+ full** |\n| Bounty Hunter | Read Lies | Insight | **16+** |\n| Thief | Lockpicking | Sleight of Hand | **16+** |\n| Thief (Lord of Thieves) | Lockpicking | Sleight of Hand | **10+** |\n| Thief | Liar's Perfume | Deception | **16+** |\n| Slaver | Break Will | Intimidation | **16+** |\n| Slaver | Truth Compulsion | Insight | **16+** |\n| Slaver | Intimidation | Intimidation | **16+** |\n| Courtier | Silver Tongue | Persuasion | **16+** |\n| Courtier | Subterfuge | Deception | **16+** |\n| Courtier | Merchant | Persuasion | **16+** |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Quick Reference: Class Ability Difficulties\n\n| Class | Ability | RPR Skill | Required Result |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| Sorcerer | Tier I · Intent Reading | Insight | **12+** |\n| Sorcerer | Tier II · Mind Control | Arcana | **16+** |\n| Sorcerer | Tier III · Memory Erasure | Arcana | **16+** |\n| Sorcerer | Tier IV · Invisibility | Arcana | **16+** |\n| Wise | Level I · Aura Reading | Insight | **12+** |\n| Wise | Level II · Divine Healing | Religion | **16+** |\n| Wise | Level III · Purification | Religion | **16+** |\n| Wise | Level IV · Divine Blessing | Religion | **16+** |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Quick Reference: Mastery Rewards\n\n| Profession | Requirement | Mastery Reward |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bard | Hired for **5 separate events** | **Famous Bard** tag; public reputation recognition |\n| Bounty Hunter | **10 successful Bounty Hunts** | **Master Hunter**; Tracking cooldown **24h → 12h** |\n| Medic | **20 successful treatments** | **Mighty Healer**; Revitalize **2/day** |\n| Fighter | **15 valid PvP wins** | **Unstoppable** tag; public reputation recognition; Battle Ready **12h → 8h** |\n| Thief | **10 successful property robberies** | **Lord of Thieves**; Lockpicking **16+ → 10+** |\n| Alchemist | Potion sales to **30 players outside own clan** | **Master Alchemist**; each special potion **2/day** |\n| Slaver | Successfully Broken **8 characters** | **Nightmare of Slaves**; Intimidation Trigger **1 week → 2 weeks** |\n| Courtier | **15 successful Silver Tongue scenes** | **Crest of Esteem**; Silver Tongue **12h → 6h** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Important Limits\n\n- RPR does not replace mechanical PvP.\n- A successful normal RP roll does not automatically remove another player's agency.\n- Consent rules still apply to all consent-sensitive content.\n- A Profession/Class ability only creates the special effect written in that ability's rules.\n- Dice do not create information that could not reasonably exist in the scene.\n- Staff may reduce, deny or contextualize information when a roll is technically high but the RP provides no believable basis for the requested result.\n- Profession Mastery evidence must show real, meaningful scenes rather than mechanical farming.\n- `/act name`, disguises and identity-hiding mechanics are not bypassed by Famous Bard or Unstoppable reputation recognition.\n\n"};
